-- title:
--   Proposition 3.1 — a universally measurable selection $\zeta(x)\in\tilde{\mathcal S}_\star(x)$ is $\rho_x[\pi]$ for one policy $\pi$
-- statement:
--   In the Borel-space MDP with analytic constraint graph $\Gamma$, let $\mathcal S_\star\in\{\mathcal S,\mathcal S_m,\mathcal S_s\}$ and let $\zeta:\mathbb X\to\mathcal P(\Omega)$ be a universally measurable mapping with $\zeta(x)\in\tilde{\mathcal S}_\star(x)$ for all $x\in\mathbb X$. Then there is a policy $\pi\in\Pi$ such that
--   1. $\rho_x[\pi]=\zeta(x)$ for all $x\in\mathbb X$;
--   2. for $\mathcal S_\star=\mathcal S_m$ or $\mathcal S_s$, $\pi$ is semi-Markov or semi-stationary, respectively.
--
--   If, in addition, $\zeta(x)\in\tilde{\mathcal S}'_\star(x)$ for all $x$, then $\pi$ can be taken to be nonrandomized (keeping 1 and 2).
--
--   Thus a single policy realizes a whole measurable family of feasible strategic measures, one for each initial state; this is how optimal or $\epsilon$-optimal selections are turned into policies in Theorem 3.3.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - reading: "π can be taken to be nonrandomized" → there is a nonrandomized $\pi$ that also satisfies 1 and 2; reason: the stronger of the two readings, and the one the proof gives (the construction keeps the class)
--   - encoding: $\zeta$ universally measurable for the Borel $\sigma$-algebra of the weak topology on $\mathcal P(\Omega)$ → preimages of the sets measurable for Mathlib's $\sigma$-algebra generated by $p\mapsto p(B)$ are universally measurable; reason: the two $\sigma$-algebras coincide for Borel spaces (Bertsekas–Shreve Prop. 7.25), and in general the hypothesis is only weaker
--   - encoding: semi-Markov and semi-stationary policies as kernels depending only on $(x_0,x_n)$ → kernels factoring through universally measurable kernels on $\mathbb A$ given $\mathbb X^2$; reason: the two descriptions give the same policies
--   - encoding: analytic sets as the empty set or images of Borel subsets of Polish spaces under Borel maps (p. 5) → Mathlib's `AnalyticSet` (empty or a continuous image of the Baire space); reason: the two agree for subsets of a Borel space (Bertsekas–Shreve Prop. 7.41)
--   - encoding: $\rho_{p_0}[\pi]$ as the restriction of $\mathbb P^\pi_{p_0}$ to $\mathcal B(\Omega)$ → the predicate `IsStrategicMeasure M π p₀ P` ($x_0\sim p_0$, $a_n$ given $h_n$ follows $\mu_n$, $x_{n+1}$ given $h_n'$ follows $q$); reason: the predicate characterizes exactly that measure (compare Lemma 5.1), which exists and is unique by the milestone `strategicMeasure_existsUnique`
--   - generalization: the model includes a lower semianalytic one-stage cost $c$ → the model has no cost; reason: the statement does not involve $c$, so every model of the paper is an instance
-- source:
--   Yu, arXiv:2206.06492v3, Proposition 3.1, p. 8

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_BertsekasShreve_AnalyticSelection_BorelSpace
import Definitions.Def_BertsekasShreve_BorelInfinite_Analytic
import Definitions.Def_YuStrategic_Optimality_StrategicSets

namespace YuStrategic.Optimality

open MeasureTheory BertsekasShreve.AnalyticSelection

/-- **Proposition 3.1** (Yu, arXiv:2206.06492v3, p. 8). Let `S⋆ ∈ {S, S_m, S_s}`. Let
`ζ : X → P(Ω)` be a universally measurable mapping such that `ζ(x) ∈ S̃⋆(x)` for all `x ∈ X`.
Then there exists a policy `π ∈ Π` such that
1. `ρₓ[π] = ζ(x)` for all `x ∈ X`;
2. for `S⋆ = S_m` or `S_s`, `π` is semi-Markov or semi-stationary, respectively.

If, in addition, `ζ(x) ∈ S̃′⋆(x)` for all `x`, then `π` can be taken to be nonrandomized (with
1 and 2 still holding).

**Formalization Note.** "Universally measurable" is
`BertsekasShreve.BorelInfinite.IsUniversallyMeasurableFun`: the preimage of every measurable set
of `P(Ω)` (Mathlib's σ-algebra generated by `p ↦ p(B)`, the Borel σ-algebra of the weak
topology for a Borel space) is universally measurable. `ρₓ[π] = ζ(x)` is
`IsStrategicMeasure M π δₓ (ζ x)`. The class requirement is `κ.semiMem`: no constraint for `S`,
semi-Markov for `S_m`, semi-stationary for `S_s`. -/
theorem proposition_3_1 {X A : Type} [TopologicalSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X] [BorelSpace X]
    [IsBorelSpace X] [TopologicalSpace A] [MeasurableSpace A] [BorelSpace A] [IsBorelSpace A]
    (M : Model X A) (κ : PolicyClass) (ζ : X → ProbabilityMeasure (Path X A))
    (hζ : BertsekasShreve.BorelInfinite.IsUniversallyMeasurableFun ζ)
    (hζS : ∀ x, (x, ζ x) ∈ stratSetTilde M κ) :
    (∃ π : Policy M, κ.semiMem π ∧ ∀ x, IsStrategicMeasure M π (diracPM x) (ζ x)) ∧
      ((∀ x, (x, ζ x) ∈ stratSetTilde' M κ) →
        ∃ π : Policy M, κ.semiMem π ∧ π.IsNonrandomized ∧
          ∀ x, IsStrategicMeasure M π (diracPM x) (ζ x)) := by sorry

end YuStrategic.Optimality
